    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but honestly my doctor's office is so far away and it's such a hassle to get an appointment. i'm pretty sure it's just my blood pressure acting up or something with my electrolytes like i thought. would it be okay if i just tried taking some extra magnesium and some salt in my water for a couple of days to see if that fixes the fluttering and the dizzy spells before i bother making an appointment? i'd rather just handle it myself if it's something simple.",
